{
  "requirement": "No prompt, tool result, or tool error the harness gives the model MUST state a\nline number or line range of a project source, except within source text it\nquotes and where a tool error repeats a line number the model supplied. The\nharness MUST identify a source location by file and outline selector under\n{cite}`requirements.references.outline_selectors` instead.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.authoring.no_line_numbers`. The outline-selector format in `requirements.references.outline_selectors` is cited context and was not reassessed.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. Tool results must give no line number or range of a project source.\n2. Tool errors must give none either, except where the error repeats a number the model supplied.\n3. Prompts must give none.\n4. Quoted source text is exempt.\n5. Locations must be identified by file and outline selector.\n\n**Tool results**\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[reading_records_only_delivered_sources_and_their_terms]` asserts that an item read and an end-of-file line-range read carry item and kind but no start or end line fields. It also asserts that recorded inputs equal `outline_input` (file, selector, hash).\n- `fn[line_range_reads_record_the_innermost_covering_nodes]` asserts that line-range reads return selectors, including `line@…` selectors for plain text, and no line fields. It covers Rust and plain-text files and nested nodes.\n- `fn[search_merges_context_windows_and_respects_ignore_rules]` and `fn[separate_windows_in_one_node_are_divided_by_an_elision_line]` assert that search matches carry file, item, kind and lines with only text and matched. The second test pins the exact entry shape.\n- `fn[outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs]` asserts that outline entries have item, kind, name and children, and no line field.\n- `fn[references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs]` asserts exact site objects with file and item only.\n- `src/sites.rs#mod[tests]/fn[sites_are_the_innermost_nodes_of_site_matches_and_violations_within_them]` asserts that `matches_value()` has only kind, query, item and text. The internal line fields of a site are not what the model receives.\n\n**Tool errors**\n- `src/authoring/line_numbers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_drop_the_source_line_of_a_parse_error]` tests `without_source_lines` directly:\n  - A parse-error line position is dropped and the file becomes `file#`.\n  - A TOML or YAML \"at line, column\" position is dropped.\n  - A `file:N:` diagnostic and a second file-position inside the message both become `file#`.\n  - The model-supplied single-line and range forms in the \"is not an inclusive range\" error are kept unchanged. This is the exception the requirement allows.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_give_the_model_no_line_numbers_it_did_not_supply]` is an end-to-end test of the harness.\n  - A past-the-end read repeats only the supplied start line.\n  - A real parse error does contain a line position.\n  - The request the model actually receives, after `assess` runs, contains \"cannot parse\" but no line position.\n\n**Prompts**\n- `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` asserts the exact mandatory-input JSON, which has no line fields. `model_mandatory_inputs` only adds `github_issues`.\n- `site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site` checks the site prompt's match descriptions, which carry kind, query and item selector with no lines. It also checks that the prompt reaches the model.\n- `submission_descriptions_explain_arguments_and_successful_completion` checks that the submission tool descriptions say \"outline selectors\" and \"never line numbers\". This covers the instruction to identify locations by file and selector.\n\n**Gaps**\nI found none. Quoted source text is legitimately unchecked. The error rewriting is regex-based, so unusual error shapes are not enumerated. The requirement names no such shapes, and the tested forms (parse, query, TOML, YAML, duplicate declaration, supplied range) cover the sources the harness reports.",
  "references": "5f07d59d3d70ca6a503110d2a797133c2b9f1eafd54fb53e7ee2fb02587ec51a",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.authoring.no_line_numbers",
